  "name": "Elijah",
  "title": "The Prophet from Tishbe",
  "era": "divided-kingdom",
  "lifespan": "c. 900–850 BC",
  "summary": "Elijah was one of Israel's most powerful prophets, active during King Ahab's reign. He is known for his confrontation with the prophets of Baal on Mount Carmel, his miracles, and his dramatic ascent to heaven in a chariot of fire. He represents the prophetic tradition that met Jesus at the Transfiguration.",
